<title>ITALY: Rinascente reports rise in 96 profit.</title>
<headline>Rinascente reports rise in 96 profit.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ending Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>(In billion lire unless stated)</p>
<p>    Cons net profit			  92.2 vs 76.2</p>
<p>    Cons cashflow			   371.9 vs 324.2</p>
<p>    Ord div				200 lire vs 100 lire</p>
<p>    Savings share div		  200 lire vs 160 lire</p>
<p>    Cons turnover			   7,169 vs 6,703.8</p>
<p>    Net financial income		   26.5 vs 63.6</p>
<p>    Parent co turnover		  4,979.4 vs 4,670</p>
<p>    Group net financial position     353.2  vs 490.4</p>
<p>    Group extraordinary charges	    20 vs 55.6</p>
<p>Note - Holders of savings shares will receive an additional dividend of 120 lire. The company said in a statement that parent net profit of 6.3 billion lire was not comparable with the previous year's 60.2 billion lire because of the altered distribution of liquidity between companies within the group. Parent operating profit at 17.8 billion lire was also not comparable with 1995's figure of 130.4 billion lire for the same reason. -- Milan newsroom +392 66129450</p>
</text>
